  "worked_solution": "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|A|=3,\\,|B|=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(B)| & ={2}^{|B|}={2}^{0}=1, \\\\ |P(P(B))| & ={2}^{|P(B)|}={2}^{1}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A\\times P(P(B)))| & ={2}^{|A\\times P(P(B))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|A|\\,\\cdot \\,|P(P(B))|} \\\\  & ={2}^{3\\cdot 2} \\\\  & ={2}^{6} \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
